data.content:
## What Changed

.NET 10's `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgrades to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which targets **OpenAPI v3.1**. This is a major object-model rewrite:

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. | `JsonNode` (`JsonValue.Create(...)`) | `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` namespace removed entirely |
| `new OpenApiSecurityScheme { Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ..., Id = ... } }` | `new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("id")` | References are now dedicated types in `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References` |
| `property.Nullable = false` | Remove `JsonSchemaType.Null` from `property.Type` | OpenAPI 3.1 uses JSON Schema's `type: [T, "null"]` instead of `nullable` |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

### Summary of each fix

1. **`OpenApiString("1.0")`** → **`JsonValue.Create("1.0")`** — `Schema.Example` is now `JsonNode`.
2. **`OpenApiSecurityScheme { Reference = ... }`** → **`new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2")`** — one-liner that replaces the old reference pattern.
3. **`Nullable = false`** → **`Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null`** — strips the `Null` flag from the JSON Schema type enum.
4. **Usings**: drop `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any`, add `System.Text.Json.Nodes` and `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References`.
